Written by Eric Rouviere
Started Oct 2024

A fully linear elastic network model that offers a different implementation than v15.
Here mutations change both a springs stiffness, but also change the tension along a bond. U(r) = 0.5 r'Hr + f'r.
This allows mutations to change the structure which enables binding sites to change the geometry to fit ligand. 
Ligand binding is modeled by the addition of first and second polynomidal to simulation applied force and stiffness.

As with v15 This model is used to to study if selection for evolvability (fluctuating environments) leads to latent allostery in a model without a bistable switch. 

